Java Practice Exercises

Exercise 1 – Age Check
Create a program that asks the user for their age.
If the person is 18 or older, print "You are an adult."
Otherwise, print "You are under 18."

Exercise 2 – Employee Salary
Create a program that asks for an employee's salary.
If the salary is greater than €3,000, print "High salary."
Otherwise, print "Standard salary."

Exercise 3 – Employee Class
Create an Employee class with the following attributes:

name
age
salary

In the Main class, create one employee object and assign values to its attributes.

Print the employee's information.

Exercise 4 – Employee Status
Create an Employee class with:

name
age
salary

Create an employee object.

If the employee's salary is €3,000 or more, print "Senior salary."
    Otherwise, print "Standard salary."

Exercise 5 – Product Class
Create a Product class with:

name
price
quantity

Create one product object.

If the quantity is greater than 10, print "Large stock."
Otherwise, print "Low stock."

Exercise 6 – Bank Account
Create a BankAccount class with:

accountHolder
balance

Create getters and setters for both attributes.

Create an account object and use the setters to assign values.

Use the getters to print the account holder and balance.

Exercise 7 – Employee Validation
Create an Employee class with:

name
age
salary

Use private attributes with getters and setters.

Create an employee object.

If the employee is 18 or older and their salary is greater than €2,500, print "Employee approved."
Otherwise, print "Employee does not meet the requirements."

Exercise 8 – Vehicle Rental
Create a Vehicle class with:

brand
model
dailyRate
available

Use private attributes with getters and setters.

Create one vehicle object.

If the vehicle is available and the daily rate is less than €100, print "Vehicle available for rental."
Otherwise, print "Vehicle is not available."

Exercise 9 – Bicycle Rental
Create a Bicycle class with:

brand
model
hourlyRate
available

Use private attributes with getters and setters.

Create a bicycle object.

Ask the user how many hours they want to rent the bicycle.

Calculate the total rental cost.

If the bicycle is available and the rental cost is less than €50, print the rental information.

Otherwise, print "Rental cannot be completed."

Exercise 10 – Employee Management System
Create an Employee class with:

name
age
department
salary
active

Use private attributes with getters and setters.

In the Main class, create two employee objects.

Ask the user which employee they want to check.

Display the selected employee's information.

If the employee is active and their age is 18 or older and their salary is greater than €2,500, print "Employee meets all requirements."

Otherwise, print "Employee does not meet all requirements."